Use Linux unprivileged ping sockets instead of raw sockets.

SOCK_DGRAM/IPPROTO_ICMP needs no CAP_NET_RAW when net.ipv4.ping_group_range
covers the calling user, which lets the helper run as a normal user. The
kernel delivers only this socket's replies, strips the IP header, and owns
the echo identifier, so the offsets and the reply matching change with it.

TTL comes from the IP header and is no longer available; it reports 0.

